<title>USA: Interneuron to buy back shares, take charge.</title>
<headline>Interneuron to buy back shares, take charge.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interneuron Pharmaceuticals Inc said on Thursday it will repurchase up to 200,000 common shares of its majority-owned subsidiary, Intercardia Inc.</p>
<p>The repurchases, to be made on the open market, would result in a charge to Interneuron's results.</p>
<p>Intercardia currently has 6.7 million shares outstanding, of which 4.0 million were held by Interneuron. Intercardia shares closed at 18 after trading on Thursday.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
